{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_bbf049a53bae4bd6b7b11bf720ea3aac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_830cd6e3f84c14e325d1986c8042ea17ec12ffa4249969b18bfbe7f60b1737dc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"zoo-code-org/zoo-code@ba46d1f34a5b snapshot 2a1006e3c37b084d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2f0da42d88e7d3ff003ffa69a2246732b49c20357847882750a74d2bcdf6a264"],"source_ids":["src_02de340ef9b457cfb91670ed2dab85b8"],"text":"In Zoo Code Cloud proxy mode, code and prompts transit Zoo Code servers only for forwarding to the upstream provider and are not stored; otherwise data goes directly to the chosen AI provider.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bbf049a53bae4bd6b7b11bf720ea3aac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_bbf049a53bae4bd6b7b11bf720ea3aac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a3a9f3c88d772abd158c512f923556f9f9a32649349928e3129f44e476843c09","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"zoo-code-org/zoo-code@ba46d1f34a5b snapshot 2a1006e3c37b084d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_46aa994cea98f72392601a8a9af829e3753acbb44209fe3b98385ffe5affbc1f"],"source_ids":["src_02de340ef9b457cfb91670ed2dab85b8"],"text":"Per the privacy policy, telemetry is enabled by default but can be opted out via settings, and users can run models locally to avoid sending data to third parties.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bbf049a53bae4bd6b7b11bf720ea3aac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_bbf049a53bae4bd6b7b11bf720ea3aac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a8982545176872a3499638959b0012781a1268aadcceaea7be2a5b5acd031cc4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"zoo-code-org/zoo-code@ba46d1f34a5b snapshot 2a1006e3c37b084d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2bf8abf74834c3e0ccf633bdc434fa111c697c2a3fa8381beed499b437053239","slc_570e6f1cd321242c8447eb953fa87582a530fc3f3ebeccd921a958d965c8a092","slc_f6a40e155cf0e1ad56bdd3f3fca190e03fe2b2c83e29e967ecc4168e0e835164"],"source_ids":["src_edb2d22b86485799b0abef2c550867c1"],"text":"Repository development practice: a bounded TypeScript model-check suite (pnpm lifecycle:model-check) runs six submodels covering task delegation, shared-store concurrency, provider handoff, cleanup, parser scoping, and completion persistence, and is the model-check entry point in the compile CI job.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bbf049a53bae4bd6b7b11bf720ea3aac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_bbf049a53bae4bd6b7b11bf720ea3aac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ea1b08c665096b9a098a507087758e8f3dc252f275a0ba4905fce4f3ac5d7b47","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"zoo-code-org/zoo-code@ba46d1f34a5b snapshot 2a1006e3c37b084d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0ef36c6df91d9167d2312ff253687d162f43ed79299da8d2f18c27b48bb861ef"],"source_ids":["src_f9e1bc5eb05f5f1f951c5590d5f9ee81"],"text":"Additions over Roo Code include Semble semantic code search, stronger orchestrator delegation with parent/child task recovery, and a Destructive Command Guard that blocks dangerous commands during autonomous runs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bbf049a53bae4bd6b7b11bf720ea3aac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_bbf049a53bae4bd6b7b11bf720ea3aac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ee205600f0cee36ceb43bb435d30b7b7ab404feb16bcb0f81a5796df5306be30","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"zoo-code-org/zoo-code@ba46d1f34a5b snapshot 2a1006e3c37b084d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_27a794203ed84bff1993b5b1ecacc56138f9cebd46afe3199cf0ceeca23ca3b8","slc_7f403c1a800d2133dd0651052ef8f0a3056ce4eb4c1d8635d5ccdb28ebc89cee","slc_cd7b6bcbd37592f60aa4e9c8f8726a9d0424ec6f5e28f57e0bb61c81b181e2e2"],"source_ids":["src_edb2d22b86485799b0abef2c550867c1"],"text":"Repository development practice: the shared-store model tracks two known-unsafe witnesses as issue-keyed ratchets (#1469 stale completion after handoff, #1021 stale live-task save after abandonment), and CI fails if witnesses or landmarks change.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bbf049a53bae4bd6b7b11bf720ea3aac"}
